Package: sisura-boot-hardening
Version: 0.2.1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: The Sisura Authors <ahmetatakan.tech@gmail.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Suggests: grub2-common
Description: Sisura Linux boot loader hardening
 GRUB configuration for installed Sisura systems:
  - kernel hardening parameters (slab_nomerge, init_on_alloc, ...) on every
    Linux boot entry
  - optional GRUB password (sisura-grub-password): editing boot entries,
    the GRUB shell and recovery entries require it, while the default
    entry still boots unattended
  - virtio-gpu driver in the initramfs, so the LUKS prompt is visible on
    the screen of VMs with a virtio-gpu display (UTM, QEMU)
 .
 The GRUB parts do nothing on systems without GRUB (VMs booted directly
 by QEMU).
